    "continent": "Oceania",
    "notes_unique": "Most climate-vulnerable nation (average elevation 2m above sea level, highest point 3m (Banaba excepted), existential threat, some atolls already submerging, saltwater intrusion, President Tong purchased land in Fiji for relocation, 'climate refugees', Paris Agreement poster child); largest exclusive economic zone ratio (3.5 million km² ocean vs 811 km² land, 33 atolls + 1 raised coral island across 3 island groups spanning 3,500km); Battle of Tarawa (November 20-23, 1943, US Marines vs Japanese, 1,000+ US dead in 76 hours, one of bloodiest Pacific Theatre battles, Betio fortifications); Banaba (Ocean Island, phosphate mining 1900-79, British/Australian/NZ companies stripped island bare, Banabans forcibly relocated to Rabi Fiji, environmental devastation, colonial exploitation epitome); nuclear testing (Christmas Island/Kiritimati, British thermonuclear tests 1957-62, Operation Grapple, servicemen exposed, health effects); International Date Line (Kiribati moved dateline 1995 so all islands on same day, Line Islands UTC+14 first place to see new year); Phoenix Islands Protected Area (largest marine protected area when declared 2008, ~408k km², UNESCO); copra (dried coconut, primary export historically); te maneaba (community meeting house, traditional governance); seafaring (traditional navigation); fishing licenses (major revenue source, tuna); remittances (seafarers abroad on merchant ships); one of world's poorest countries; overcrowded South Tarawa (~60k on small atoll)",
